Function
A function is a block of code that performs a specific task.

Function Declaration
A function declaration tells the compiler about a function before it is used.

Function Definition
A function definition contains the actual code of a function.

Function Call
A function call is used to execute a function.

Return Type
Return type specifies the type of value returned by a function.

Parameter
A parameter is a variable that receives a value in a function.

Argument
An argument is a value passed to a function when it is called.

Return Statement
The return statement sends a value back from a function and ends its execution.

Void Function
A void function is a function that does not return any value.

Library Function
A library function is a predefined function provided by the C library.

User-Defined Function
A user-defined function is a function created by the programmer.

Recursive Function
A recursive function is a function that calls itself.

Call by Value
Call by value passes a copy of the value to a function.

Call by Reference
Call by reference passes the address of a variable to a function.

Local Variable
A local variable is a variable declared inside a function or block.

Global Variable
A global variable is a variable declared outside all functions.

Function with Arguments
A function with arguments receives values from the calling function.

Function without Arguments
A function without arguments does not receive values from the calling function.

Function with Return Value
A function with a return value sends a value back to the calling function.

Function without Return Value
A function without a return value does not send any value back.